      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T03:58:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These values don\u0027t match the documentation in the AIDL file, which says the code of the ServiceSpecificException are a UNIX error code. (1 is EPERM)\n\nAlso they are not useful:\n- They are all \u003d\u003d 1 so they pass no information to the caller\n- Even if they were different, the names just encode the operation that failed. But the caller already knows the operation that failed, because they know what method they called.\n\nWould suggest making the behaviour match the documentation, and exposing a UNIX error to the caller. That allows us to pass back useful information, if not now, then at least in the future.\n\nOther possibilities include\n- Making the methods return a boolean success/failure instead of throwing, but that seems worse than passing an error.\n- In the AIDL file, defining specific BLOCK_PORT_* AIDL int constants for the codes that can appears in the ServiceSpecificException, and then using them here. That doesn\u0027t seem to provide much value.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 48
      },
